{"name":"Braces / orthodontics for jaw shape","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Braces and other orthodontic appliances align teeth and bite, and in growing patients can guide jaws. People interested in appearance discuss them for a better profile and smile, often alongside jaw surgery.","Appliances apply sustained force to move teeth through bone, and palatal expanders and headgear can alter jaw alignment or airflow. Clinicians learned that perfect occlusion alone does not ensure good facial appearance. Severe jaw discrepancies may need surgery combined with orthodontics. Registered trials mostly address alignment speed, sleep and airway rather than facial attractiveness."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Treatment is planned by an orthodontist and runs for months to years, with retainers afterward. For skeletal problems it is paired with jaw surgery before and after the operation."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Decalcification and decay with poor hygiene are described, and relapse is frequent, so retainers are often recommended. Facial-aesthetic outcomes are less studied than dental ones."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"[New treatment modalities for patients with cleft lip, jaw and palate].","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2247367/","source":"Den Norske tannlaegeforenings tidende","year":1990,"cites":0,"kind":null},{"title":"Apparatus for determining the desired position of teeth","url":"https://europepmc.org/article/PAT/US4610629","source":null,"year":1986,"cites":0,"kind":null},{"title":"Device for determining the desired position of the teeth","url":"https://europepmc.org/article/PAT/EP0141014","source":null,"year":1985,"cites":0,"kind":null},{"title":"[ORTHODONTICS, JAW SURGERY, FUNCTIONAL ORTHODONTICS].","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14290120/","source":"Deutsche Stomatologie","year":1965,"cites":0,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"New therapeutic strategies in osteoa